A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
NOTE - COMMAND-SEQUENCE COMMENT

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    NOTE [text]

Does nothing and returns to the command processor. Use it to annotate a
command sequence. Example: NOTE BEGIN FILE CHECK

It does not send or save a note. Use public MESSAGE to leave a note for
the sysop.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
